A||N||29||FieroKyle||Annoying Seat Belt Flapping with Windows Down||||1||
Z||000000||FieroKyle||07-15-2001||01:26 AM||||Ok when I am cruising and I have the passenger window down, without a passenger, the seat belt flops all around and makes a really annoying sound. Does your guys fieros do this? Anyone have any suggestions? It isn't loose and its where its supposed to be. Its just that belt flaps between the seat and the door and its annoying as hell after a while.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign_1.jpg"> <BR>My Fast 'n Black Car<P>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||07-15-2001||01:29 AM||||Normal Fiero trait.  All of mine do this.. if it gets really annoying I just wrap the seatbelt around the passenger seat headrest.  Also works with an annoying passenger.. just subtract the "seat headrest" part and substitute "head"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steven||07-15-2001||01:34 AM||||I have been know to just plug the belt in to the buckle. Kind of like what your passenger would do if they were there.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroKyle||07-15-2001||01:35 AM||||I do that, but it sorta looks dumb. I am hoping for a best solution.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Steven||07-15-2001||01:39 AM||||Wish I could give you one. The other answer is to roll up the window till it stops flapping. It stops at about a third up the way up on mine. The real problem about hooking the belt is if you pick up a friend. Tring to explain to them why it is like that.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroKyle||07-15-2001||01:53 AM||||been there done that, I might have to look into a seat belt hook like on new cars.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Galen||07-15-2001||02:32 AM||||Just stick a stuffed bear and buckle it in.. looks kinda 'odd' but heck, aren't we 'odd'?<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"It may be the opinion of the court, but its still wrong"</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><A HREF="http://www.ezRpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>ezRpg Networks</A></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroKyle||07-15-2001||02:34 AM||||I am not trying to be gay, I am trying to get a flapping noise out of my misery.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fierokid87||07-15-2001||03:45 AM||||Well what I would do is just lean the seat foward run the seat belt behind the seat, and hook it into the buckle.  Lean the seat back to its original posion and that should do it.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Galen||07-15-2001||06:41 AM||||Keep the window rolled up, better gas milage<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"It may be the opinion of the court, but its still wrong"</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><A HREF="http://www.ezRpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>ezRpg Networks</A></FONT>||||reg||1
