Z||000011||Will||07-15-2001||04:47 PM||||Put a beautiful woman with large breasts in the passenger seat. This will keep the belt tight and prevent the flappin' noise.||||reg||12
Z||000012||Toddster||07-15-2001||04:53 PM||||Hit the local wrecking yard. I think it was the Cadillac Cimmarron (sp?) or something like that that has these plastic sleeves that fit nicely over the tops of the belt. <P>Flapus Eradicatus.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Good luck||||reg||1
Z||000013||FieroKyle||07-15-2001||06:45 PM||||Keep the window up for better gas mileage? Thats a solution? So turning on the air conditioner in place of it doesn't use more gas? Just wondered, lol =). I like the windows down, and can't hurt gas mileage THAT much. A caddy cimarron? Should be a lot of those in the junkyards. I know they were on my mom's old Envoy those belt hooks.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Ed||07-15-2001||08:12 PM||||Running the air instead of having the windows down DOES increase gas milage according to most accounts.  "Drag" and all that.  Especially in the "recirc." position.||||reg||1
Z||000015||FieroHeather||07-15-2001||09:25 PM||||Grinthock has me sit in his passenger's seat--fixes the problem  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  And no, Im not a big breasted woman Will!!  But I do do the trick just fine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>And Standard, I resent that remark about the passenger and the seatbelt thing!!  The seatbelt cuts in ehough without wraping it around my head  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||7
